================================================================================
 !!! FLAG-NUMBERING GOTCHA (do NOT blindly copy CNan's "2 {sta}.hph") !!!
================================================================================
 The disp-line flag meanings DIFFER between versions:

   flag | OUR version (CALmodel.C readdisp1) | CNan version
   -----+------------------------------------+---------------------
    1   | fundamental phase                  | fundamental phase
    2   | GROUP velocity                     | HIGHER-mode phase
    3   | ellipticity (H/V)                  | ellipticity
    4   | (unused)                           | GROUP velocity

 In our code flag 2 == group. So either:
   (i)  adopt CNan numbering: 2 = higher phase, move group to 4, OR
   (ii) assign a NEW flag (e.g. 5 = higher phase) to keep group=2 intact.
 Whatever is chosen MUST be consistent across:
   readdisp1 (CALmodel.C), 00_make_file_control.sh, and SetupData.

